item.text:
`OnNewMail()` should only ingest and validate incoming mail, then update app state. It should not compute odometry or publish the result, because mail delivery timing is event-driven and may include only `NAV_X`, only `NAV_Y`, multiple stale/partial updates, or batches whose ordering does not represent one clean navigation sample.

A safer pattern is:

```cpp
bool Odometry::OnNewMail(MOOSMSG_LIST &NewMail)
{
  for(const auto& msg : NewMail) {
    const std::string key = msg.GetKey();

    if(key == "NAV_X") {
      m_curr_x = msg.GetDouble();
      m_got_x = true;
    } else if(key == "NAV_Y") {
      m_curr_y = msg.GetDouble();
      m_got_y = true;
    }
  }

  return true;
}

bool Odometry::Iterate()
{
  if(!m_got_x || !m_got_y)
    return true;

  if(!m_have_prev) {
    m_prev_x = m_curr_x;
    m_prev_y = m_curr_y;
    m_have_prev = true;
    Notify("ODOM_DIST", m_total);
    return true;
  }

  const double dx = m_curr_x - m_prev_x;
  const double dy = m_curr_y - m_prev_y;
  const double delta = hypot(dx, dy);

  m_total += delta;
  m_prev_x = m_curr_x;
  m_prev_y = m_curr_y;

  Notify("ODOM_DIST", m_total);
  return true;
}
```

Conceptually:

- `OnNewMail()`:
  - Reads MOOS variables.
  - Checks keys and types.
  - Stores latest `NAV_X` / `NAV_Y`.
  - Sets flags such as `m_got_x`, `m_got_y`.
  - Does not publish derived output.

- `Iterate()`:
  - Runs at the app tick rate.
  - Decides whether enough state exists to compute.
  - Computes distance from the previous complete position.
  - Updates previous-position state.
  - Publishes `ODOM_DIST`.

The key fix is separating asynchronous input handling from periodic app behavior. Odometry should be based on complete position samples, not on whatever subset of mail happened to arrive in one `OnNewMail()` call.
